# Personal listening data: the export carries a full play history for every
# track -- counts, last-played and added dates. Kept locally because the tool
# needs it, never committed.
#
# Every rule here is a whole line. Git does NOT support trailing comments in
# .gitignore: `data/Geoblocked.txt  # optional` matches a file whose name ends
# in "  # optional" and silently protects nothing. That mistake put 241 tracks
# of listening history into this repository's history.
data/Geoblocked.txt
data/list.tsv
data/state.json

# Any copy of the index is the same history under another name. Backing it up
# before a destructive pass is prescribed (CLAUDE.md), so the copies WILL be
# made -- and `data/list.tsv` alone does not match `data/list.tsv.bak-...`.
data/list.tsv.*

# The whole-library snapshot and the archive's index: the same listening
# history as the index above, for every track instead of the dead ones.
data/catalog.tsv
data/catalog.tsv.*
data/archive.json

# Download staging; Music copies imports into its own Media folder
work/

# Spotify app credentials -- the user's own, supplied locally
data/spotify.json
